                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 13.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Imperial decrees published in the Pekin Gazette July
                        12, 1900.</hi></head>
                <p>The death of General Meh Shih Cheng.—Though he had done much to train the troops,
                    yet on the occasion he made many blunders. We deprived him of his rank, but
                    retained him in command, hoping he would redeem his faults, but on the eleventh
                    moon, (July 9), he fell at the head of his forces.</p>
                <p>Note by Yu Lu in the defense of Tientsin.—The gentry of Tientsin have stated that
                    after several days of hard fighting our troops are sorely pressed. They ask
                    reinforcements, and measures are proposed for their relief.</p>
                <p>A decree has been sent to the southern viceroys to hurry up troops to the
                    capital, which is described as in a state of confusion.</p>
            </div>
